/-! ## §1 — the deployed object: exactly what `EmitRotationV3.lean` prints for the key. -/

/-- **The DEPLOYED custom descriptor.** `EmitRotationV3.lean:153` iterates `v3RegistryCapOpenDep` and
prints, for each `(key, d)`,

    emitVmJson2 <| dropUnforcedPins <| hardenLastRow <| fieldsCanonical9Wire
      <| keyCanonical9Wire <| ownerFreezeWire <| d

`customVmDescriptor2R24` is member 19 of the bare cohort, so `d` is
`withDfaRcPins (gentianDeployedBareRefuse customV3)` (`v3RegistryRefused`,
`EffectVmEmitRotationV3Refused.lean:39`). It is NOT in the emitter's `availOverride` list, so
nothing else rewrites it on the way out.

⚑ **THE WRAPPER CHAIN HERE IS THE DRIVER'S, COPIED FROM `EmitRotationV3.lean:153` — and it has now
DRIFTED FROM IT TWICE, both times making the §2 pin pin AN OBJECT THE EMITTER NEVER PRINTS.** The
first drift was the two OUTERMOST wraps (`hardenLastRow`, `dropUnforcedPins`); the second was
`ownerFreezeWire` (`36541604a`, "the AFTER owner limb was welded by nothing"), which the driver
applies INNERMOST and which appends one `colEq` gate per welded owner lane; the THIRD is
`keyCanonical9Wire` (2026-08-02, the key-canonicity weld), which appends 18 range lookups and no
gate. All three are additive constraints, so `traceWidth`/`piCount`/`tables` are unmoved
(`ownerFreezeAt_traceWidth`, `keyCanonical9Wire_traceWidth` et al) and ONLY the bytes move. That is
exactly the drift a byte pin exists to catch, and it is why the golden below is taken from the
emitter's own stdout rather than composed here by hand. -/
def deployedCustomV3 : EffectVmDescriptor2 :=
  dropUnforcedPins (hardenLastRow (Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.FieldsCanonicity9Emit.fieldsCanonical9Wire
    (Dregg2.Circuit.Emit.KeyCanonicity9Emit.keyCanonical9Wire
      (ownerFreezeWire (withDfaRcPins (gentianDeployedBareRefuse customV3))))))

/-- **THE COMMITTED BYTES** — `circuit/descriptors/rotation-v3-staged-registry.tsv`, the row keyed
`customVmDescriptor2R24`, column 3, verbatim. This is the string Rust `include_str!`s and tab-scans
(`effect_vm_descriptors.rs::V3_STAGED_REGISTRY_TSV`), and the string `scripts/emit_descriptors.py`
`split_rotation` wrote there from the Lean emitter's stdout.

⚑ **RE-EMITTED 2026-08-01 at the KEY-NONET flag day**, from a HEAD-CONSISTENT build — a detached,
`git status`-clean worktree of the committed tree (`scripts/dregg-clean-build … --sha HEAD`), not a
warm lane at an older sha. The move is `trace_width` 1844 → 1866, `main` arity 1791 → 1813, and
NINE new `colEq` window-gates: the owner nonet's eight octet lanes plus the ninth (`ownerFreezeWire`,
which `deployedCustomV3` above was missing — see its docstring). Both halves were re-derived
together, the golden here and the TSV row it quotes, so the two sources still AGREE rather than one
having been retyped to match the other.

⚑ **RE-EMITTED 2026-08-02 at the KEY-CANONICITY flag day.** `keyCanonical9Wire` joined the driver's
wrapper chain, so the member gains **18 range lookups and nothing else**: eight `< 2^29` on each
block's owner octet (`293..300` / `544..551` at this member's 188-wide face) and ONE `< 2^24` on the
ninth lane (`374` / `625`). `trace_width` (1866), `piCount` (66) and the table list do NOT move —
the aux limb columns the two range widths need are allocated by the deployed interpreter PAST
`trace_width` (`MainLayout::build`), so the geometry is invariant and only the AIR fingerprint
rotates. Measured over the whole registry: every one of the 60 members is byte-identical to its
predecessor once those 18 lookups are removed, which is what makes this a minimal delta rather than
a re-lay.

⚑ **RE-EMITTED 2026-08-07 at the SEVEN-SLOT PI COMPACTION** (`docs/PI-DISPOSITION.md` §6). v1
offsets 26..32 were deleted, so `public_input_count` 66 → 59 and every published index at or above
the old `TURN_HASH_BASE` moved down by seven: `ACTOR_NONCE` 41 → 34, the four rotated commit pins
42..45 → 35..38, the sixteen `customPiExposure` pins 46..61 → 39..54, the four dsl rc pins
62..65 → 55..58. `trace_width` (1866), the `main` arity (1813) and the table list do NOT move — no
column changed, only the PI vector shortened.

⚑ **AND THIS PIN CAUGHT A REAL DEFECT WHILE IT MOVED.** `customPiExposure` wrote its four block
bases as the LITERALS `46 / 50 / 54 / 58` while `customV3.piCount` was `d.piCount + 16` — symbolic.
So the first compaction build emitted a member declaring 59 public inputs and pinning three of them
at 59, 60, 61: past the end of its own vector, which `descriptor_ir2.rs`'s parser refuses outright.
Every `piCount` `#guard` in `EffectVmEmitRotationV3` stayed green through it, because they check the
COUNT and not the INDICES. This guard, and the `declarationOnlyPins` pin in `UnforcedPiPins`, are
what went red. The bases are now `CUSTOM_EXPOSURE_PI_BASE = pi.V1_PI_COUNT + 4`.

If a regen moves it again the §2 `#guard` goes RED — that red is the pin DOING ITS JOB; re-emit from
a HEAD-consistent build and paste its stdout, never edit this literal to match.

⚑ **RE-EMITTED 2026-11-07 at the IROOT-WIDENING flag day** (`rotatedNumPreLimbs` 187 → 196):
`trace_width` 1866 → 1932, `main` arity 1813 → 1879 (+66: `APPENDIX_SPAN` +24 and six more chained
sites). Pasted from `#eval repr (emitVmJson2 deployedCustomV3)` on the flag-day build. -/
